[[:db/retract 17592186122606 :answer-field/choices 17592186122608] [:db/retract 17592186122606 :answer-field/choices 17592186122609] [:db/retract 17592186122606 :answer-field/choices 17592186122610] [:db/retract 17592186122606 :answer-field/choices 17592186122611] [:db/retract 17592186122606 :answer-field/choices 17592186122607] {:db/id 17592186124557 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-13585dd1-9ab5-5887-870c-2d899c40d4a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125001 :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xyz)$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xyz)$ is defined only when $-1\\le xyz\\le 1.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le xyz\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{1-(xyz)^{2}}}$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-(xyz)^{2} & >0 \\\\ (xyz)^{2} & <1 \\\\ |xyz| & <1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $-1<xyz<1.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domains of ${f}_{y}$ and ${f}_{z}$ are the same:\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivatives of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le xyz\\le 1\\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122606 :answer-field/correct "answer-323e1e26-806d-5103-9c5b-05be999f86f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-323e1e26-806d-5103-9c5b-05be999f86f1" "answer-66b51739-6d9c-59ee-81d0-4f21e588a03b" "answer-3f71ffa0-c375-5e54-a4b4-82c47e1862fe" "answer-ab77e5e6-52f4-5889-9394-0781e3a0ecd5" "answer-58a495bb-1535-5c0c-8153-9cddc1a1d72c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-323e1e26-806d-5103-9c5b-05be999f86f1" :answer/id #uuid "323e1e26-806d-5103-9c5b-05be999f86f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1<xyz<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66b51739-6d9c-59ee-81d0-4f21e588a03b" :answer/id #uuid "66b51739-6d9c-59ee-81d0-4f21e588a03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le xyz\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f71ffa0-c375-5e54-a4b4-82c47e1862fe" :answer/id #uuid "3f71ffa0-c375-5e54-a4b4-82c47e1862fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0<xyz<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab77e5e6-52f4-5889-9394-0781e3a0ecd5" :answer/id #uuid "ab77e5e6-52f4-5889-9394-0781e3a0ecd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58a495bb-1535-5c0c-8153-9cddc1a1d72c" :answer/id #uuid "58a495bb-1535-5c0c-8153-9cddc1a1d72c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124465 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-abe73768-66b7-589e-98db-9176084649e0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-abe73768-66b7-589e-98db-9176084649e0" :question/id #uuid "abe73768-66b7-589e-98db-9176084649e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72006" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy),$ find the set of values $(x,y)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ exists." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)$ is defined when $xy>0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{x}{xy} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ is defined only for\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}\\cap \\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4cca11fe-f3bb-53ee-b7b6-de2725b37ad7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4cca11fe-f3bb-53ee-b7b6-de2725b37ad7" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cca11fe-f3bb-53ee-b7b6-de2725b37ad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff439fa7-e5eb-53d6-8dc0-e5396941eb06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ebb0a6cd-e867-5b85-88ef-cd845e6904a8" "answer-ff439fa7-e5eb-53d6-8dc0-e5396941eb06" "answer-4d5bdc4f-f2f7-5295-b2ba-aa4588793c88" "answer-26545a18-833f-5099-8272-edbb2a66edaa" "answer-a9d10897-b8cf-5fad-b81e-91fbcac64c00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebb0a6cd-e867-5b85-88ef-cd845e6904a8" :answer/id #uuid "ebb0a6cd-e867-5b85-88ef-cd845e6904a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy<0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff439fa7-e5eb-53d6-8dc0-e5396941eb06" :answer/id #uuid "ff439fa7-e5eb-53d6-8dc0-e5396941eb06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d5bdc4f-f2f7-5295-b2ba-aa4588793c88" :answer/id #uuid "4d5bdc4f-f2f7-5295-b2ba-aa4588793c88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26545a18-833f-5099-8272-edbb2a66edaa" :answer/id #uuid "26545a18-833f-5099-8272-edbb2a66edaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9d10897-b8cf-5fad-b81e-91fbcac64c00" :answer/id #uuid "a9d10897-b8cf-5fad-b81e-91fbcac64c00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${f}_{y}$ exists everywhere on the $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339045 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy(z-1))?$\n\nI. The partial derivative with respect to $z$ is defined at $(3,2,1)$\n\nII. ${f}_{y}(1,1,2)$ is defined\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(1,2,3)$ is defined" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-13585dd1-9ab5-5887-870c-2d899c40d4a5" :question/id #uuid "13585dd1-9ab5-5887-870c-2d899c40d4a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132652" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{y{sin}^{2}⁡z}\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ where all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0$ and $z\\ne n\\pi $ where $n\\in Z.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0$ and $z\\ne n\\pi $ where $n\\in Z.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domains of ${f}_{y}$ and ${f}_{z}$ are the same:\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={D}_{{f}_{z}}=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\}\\cap \\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\} \\\\  & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d0f4a07-8c58-5c53-b0aa-71dedf0ab601"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d0f4a07-8c58-5c53-b0aa-71dedf0ab601" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d0f4a07-8c58-5c53-b0aa-71dedf0ab601" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f480f4b0-b440-57d3-be41-894b18986911" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a414987-4111-5550-9b84-35b48e518248" "answer-c4574d37-c2e2-5922-8956-3143f5bef26f" "answer-c67ec9fa-9f76-59b9-b6ed-a85557705824" "answer-ee7e5c9b-05ac-5232-9af8-bc55f1d66335" "answer-f480f4b0-b440-57d3-be41-894b18986911"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a414987-4111-5550-9b84-35b48e518248" :answer/id #uuid "9a414987-4111-5550-9b84-35b48e518248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4574d37-c2e2-5922-8956-3143f5bef26f" :answer/id #uuid "c4574d37-c2e2-5922-8956-3143f5bef26f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y>0,\\,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c67ec9fa-9f76-59b9-b6ed-a85557705824" :answer/id #uuid "c67ec9fa-9f76-59b9-b6ed-a85557705824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y>0,\\,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee7e5c9b-05ac-5232-9af8-bc55f1d66335" :answer/id #uuid "ee7e5c9b-05ac-5232-9af8-bc55f1d66335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f480f4b0-b440-57d3-be41-894b18986911" :answer/id #uuid "f480f4b0-b440-57d3-be41-894b18986911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,\\,z\\ne n\\pi \\},\\,n\\in Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268914 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2)?$\n\nI. Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(0,2)$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(1,0)$ is defined\n\nIII. ${f}_{y}(1,1)$ is defined" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5947b5e4-3c04-5937-9aec-95b10c3ffed0" :activity/id #uuid "5947b5e4-3c04-5937-9aec-95b10c3ffed0" :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048877 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-d1a2f4bc-c2ad-5ea9-bbc9-a5f92a8d1b61" "step-d34189a3-bcaf-5744-9e6b-ec97ad8307d1" "step-30fe1f41-c7f8-5010-a260-ed3ef63a4abc" "step-dd470b32-cbc1-54d2-9ca1-54631aa728a9" "step-574ad7f2-698f-50d6-8eee-36f6145d16e5"] :activity/first-step "step-d1a2f4bc-c2ad-5ea9-bbc9-a5f92a8d1b61" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d1a2f4bc-c2ad-5ea9-bbc9-a5f92a8d1b61" :step/id #uuid "d1a2f4bc-c2ad-5ea9-bbc9-a5f92a8d1b61" :step/content 17592186125001 :step/next "step-d34189a3-bcaf-5744-9e6b-ec97ad8307d1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d34189a3-bcaf-5744-9e6b-ec97ad8307d1" :step/id #uuid "d34189a3-bcaf-5744-9e6b-ec97ad8307d1" :step/content "question-abe73768-66b7-589e-98db-9176084649e0" :step/next "step-30fe1f41-c7f8-5010-a260-ed3ef63a4abc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-30fe1f41-c7f8-5010-a260-ed3ef63a4abc" :step/id #uuid "30fe1f41-c7f8-5010-a260-ed3ef63a4abc" :step/content 17592186339045 :step/next "step-dd470b32-cbc1-54d2-9ca1-54631aa728a9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd470b32-cbc1-54d2-9ca1-54631aa728a9" :step/id #uuid "dd470b32-cbc1-54d2-9ca1-54631aa728a9" :step/content "question-13585dd1-9ab5-588